  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Virginia received $109B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Contract activity included 379,915 awards, with an average award size of $286K. Obligations fell 9.9% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show obligations rising from $77.9B in FY21 to $121B in FY25, then easing to $109B in FY26. The Department of Defense led buyers with $38.8B, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $34.8B and the Department of Homeland Security with $8.6B. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. was the top vendor at $19.9B, with TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP second at $10.7B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers was the largest industry by obligations at $30.6B, with Computer Systems Design Services at $11.9B and Other Computer Related Services at $8B. These figures are contract obligations and represent fiscal year to date totals, with current-year totals partial. Use these figures to compare agency concentration, vendor market share, and industry exposure within Virginia federal contracting for the current fiscal period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal contracting spend in Virginia?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $38.8B in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $34.8B, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $8.6B. The General Services Administration, Department of Health and Human Services, and Department of Justice round out major buyers with $6.3B, $4.5B, and $3.1B respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captures the biggest share of federal contract dollars in Virginia?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. captured the largest vendor share at $19.9B. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP captured $10.7B and ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. captured $4.3B. Large defense and engineering contractors also appear among top vendors, including HUNTINGTON INGALLS INC at $3.7B and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $3.3B."
      }
    ]
  },
